WHY AGPL, AND WHY "ONLY"
------------------------

Questables is a network application.  AGPL section 13 requires that
anyone who runs a MODIFIED version as a service offers its users the
corresponding source, closing the gap the plain GPL leaves open for
hosted software.

The version is pinned to 3 with no "or later" grant.  Questables links
settlemaker into the server process, and settlemaker is GPL-3.0-only
because its own upstream -- watabou's TownGeneratorOS -- publishes no
"or later" grant.  GPLv3 section 13 permits combining a GPLv3 covered
work with version 3 of the AGPL specifically; it grants no permission
for later AGPL versions.  Offering Questables as "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
would promise a freedom the combined work cannot actually deliver, so
the upstream restriction is carried through honestly instead.


COMBINED WORK
-------------

settlemaker
    https://github.com/barrulus/settlemaker
    GPL-3.0-only, Copyright (C) 2025-2026 Barry Gill

settlemaker is imported as an ES module directly into the backend:

    server/services/settlemaker/ingestor.js
    server/services/maps/settlement-service.js

This is a combined work, not arm's-length interoperation.  Questables
consumes only the generation, GeoJSON, and tiling exports from
settlemaker's dist/ build -- geometry and data, no artwork.

settlemaker's SVG symbol library (CC-BY-4.0 with a Rendered Output
Exception) lives in that project's web/ application and is not
redistributed by Questables.  No attribution obligation arises here.


